# Global gitignore. Git reads this path by default — no core.excludesFile needed,
# it is the XDG fallback ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git/ignore). Rules here apply to EVERY
# repo on the machine, so keep them to things that are never anyone's source.

# BacklogMD keeps its backlog as plain markdown inside the project, at .backlogmd/.
# Its docs make tracking optional ("if you do not want the backlog files tracked,
# just add them to .gitignore"). Ignoring it globally means no per-repo .gitignore
# edit — and no accidental commit of agent scratch work into someone else's repo.
.backlogmd/
